+        if route in ("/api/app-control/run", "/api/app-control/step",
+                     "/api/app-control/plan"):
+            # app-control.patch (2026-10-19) - the backend half of the owner's
+            # "fuller automation inside other apps". The PC is the brain and
+            # the gate; the phone is the hands. /run checks the owner's
+            # allow-list and one atomic plan and raises ONE change_own_config
+            # card - it runs nothing. /step is the phone asking for the ONE
+            # approved step, or reporting after it; a changed screen stops the
+            # run. The feature is OFF by default and this patch adds no way to
+            # switch it on, so every refusal says so in plain words. Nothing
+            # here approves anything: the card is the only yes, and
+            # jarvis_app_control.py's own docstring has the whole contract.
+            # /plan is the same card's other way in (2026-10-20): the owner's
